    "---\n## Step 1 — Load All Four Datasets\n\nWe load four complementary datasets. Each contributes a different signal layer:\n\n| Dataset | Rows | Signal Layer |\n|---------|------|--------------|\n| **Home Credit Default Risk** | 307 511 | Demographics, income, loan amounts, bureau history |\n| **Credit Score Classification** | 100 000 | Payment discipline, EMI behaviour, debt ratios |\n| **Loan Default Prediction** | 255 347 | DTI ratios, employment duration, interest sensitivity |\n| **UPI Transactions 2024** | 250 000 | Digital payment behaviour, merchant diversity, fraud signals |\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Load datasets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nhome = pd.read_csv(\"application_train.csv\")\ncred = pd.read_csv(\"train.csv\", low_memory=False)\nloan = pd.read_csv(\"Loan_default.csv\")\nupi  = pd.read_csv(\"upi_transactions_2024.csv\")\n\nfor name, df in [(\"Home Credit\", home), (\"Credit Score\", cred),\n                  (\"Loan Default\", loan), (\"UPI Transactions\", upi)]:\n    print(f\"  {name:22s}  {df.shape[0]:>7,} rows  ×  {df.shape[1]:>3} cols\")\n\nprint(\"\\n✅  All four datasets loaded.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n## Step 2 — Define & Extract the Gig Worker Cohort\n\n### Why This Filter Matters\nStandard credit models fail gig workers because they are trained on salaried\npopulations. We must isolate the informal-income cohort **before** any feature\nengineering to avoid salaried-worker patterns contaminating the signals.\n\n### Filter Logic\n| Column | Values Used | Rationale |\n|--------|-------------|-----------|\n| `NAME_INCOME_TYPE` | Self-employed, Working | Excludes pensioners & maternity |\n| `ORGANIZATION_TYPE` | 8 gig-adjacent types | Drivers, traders, self-employed, laborers |\n| `AMT_INCOME_TOTAL` | Below **90th** percentile | Keeps genuine gig workers; excludes wealthy self-employed |\n\n> **Note on percentile choice:** We deliberately use the 90th (not 75th)\n> percentile to include creditworthy kirana owners and established auto-drivers\n> — the segment GigScore most wants to approve. The 75th percentile over-excludes\n> near-prime borrowers.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Gig worker filter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nGIG_ORG_TYPES = [\n    'Self-employed', 'Taxi / driver',\n    'Transport: type 1', 'Transport: type 2',\n    'Trade: type 1', 'Trade: type 2',\n    'Low-skill Laborers', 'Drivers'\n]\n\nincome_cap = home['AMT_INCOME_TOTAL'].quantile(0.90)   # 90th percentile\n\ngig_mask = (\n    home['NAME_INCOME_TYPE'].isin(['Self-employed', 'Working']) &\n    home['ORGANIZATION_TYPE'].isin(GIG_ORG_TYPES) &\n    (home['AMT_INCOME_TOTAL'] < income_cap)\n)\n\ngig_df = home[gig_mask].copy()\n\nn_total   = len(home)\nn_gig     = len(gig_df)\ndef_rate  = gig_df['TARGET'].mean()\n\nprint(f\"  Full Home Credit dataset : {n_total:>7,} applicants\")\nprint(f\"  Gig worker cohort        : {n_gig:>7,} applicants  ({n_gig/n_total:.1%} of total)\")\nprint(f\"  Cohort default rate      : {def_rate:.2%}\")\nprint(f\"  Income ceiling applied   : ₹{income_cap:,.0f} / year  (90th pct)\")\nprint(f\"\\n  Org type breakdown:\")\nprint(gig_df['ORGANIZATION_TYPE'].value_counts().to_string())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n## Step 3 — Home Credit Feature Engineering\n\nWe select and engineer features from the Home Credit dataset. Every feature\nmaps to a real credit-risk signal for irregular-income workers.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Base feature selection ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\nBASE_COLS = [\n    'TARGET',\n    # Financial amounts\n    'AMT_INCOME_TOTAL', 'AMT_CREDIT', 'AMT_ANNUITY', 'AMT_GOODS_PRICE',\n    # Employment & demographics\n    'DAYS_EMPLOYED', 'DAYS_BIRTH',\n    'CNT_CHILDREN', 'CNT_FAM_MEMBERS',\n    # Geography\n    'REGION_RATING_CLIENT', 'REGION_RATING_CLIENT_W_CITY',\n    'REG_CITY_NOT_WORK_CITY', 'REG_CITY_NOT_LIVE_CITY', 'LIVE_CITY_NOT_WORK_CITY',\n    # Contact flags\n    'FLAG_EMP_PHONE', 'FLAG_WORK_PHONE', 'FLAG_CONT_MOBILE', 'FLAG_EMAIL',\n    'DAYS_LAST_PHONE_CHANGE',\n    # External credit bureau scores (proxy for creditworthiness)\n    'EXT_SOURCE_1', 'EXT_SOURCE_2', 'EXT_SOURCE_3',\n    # Bureau enquiry frequency\n    'AMT_REQ_CREDIT_BUREAU_DAY', 'AMT_REQ_CREDIT_BUREAU_WEEK',\n    'AMT_REQ_CREDIT_BUREAU_MON', 'AMT_REQ_CREDIT_BUREAU_YEAR',\n    # Application timing (risk signal: late-night applications = stress)\n    'HOUR_APPR_PROCESS_START',\n    # Organisation type (kept for PLFS join later)\n    'ORGANIZATION_TYPE',\n]\n\nhf = gig_df[BASE_COLS].copy()\nprint(f\"  Base feature matrix shape: {hf.shape}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Derived features ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# --- Age & employment duration (raw days → human-readable years) -----------\nhf['age']            = hf['DAYS_BIRTH'].abs()    / 365.25\nhf['years_employed'] = hf['DAYS_EMPLOYED'].abs() / 365.25\n\n# Guard: DAYS_EMPLOYED = 365243 encodes 'unemployed' in this dataset\nhf.loc[hf['DAYS_EMPLOYED'].abs() > 50_000, 'years_employed'] = 0.0\n\n# --- Income & debt ratios --------------------------------------------------\neps = 1e-6  # avoid division-by-zero throughout\nhf['credit_income_ratio']   = hf['AMT_CREDIT']      / (hf['AMT_INCOME_TOTAL'] + eps)\nhf['annuity_income_ratio']  = hf['AMT_ANNUITY']     / (hf['AMT_INCOME_TOTAL'] + eps)\nhf['goods_income_ratio']    = hf['AMT_GOODS_PRICE']  / (hf['AMT_INCOME_TOTAL'] + eps)\nhf['credit_annuity_ratio']  = hf['AMT_CREDIT']      / (hf['AMT_ANNUITY']      + eps)\nhf['income_annuity_ratio']  = hf['AMT_INCOME_TOTAL'] / (hf['AMT_ANNUITY']     + eps)\nhf['income_credit_ratio']   = hf['AMT_INCOME_TOTAL'] / (hf['AMT_CREDIT']      + eps)\n\n# --- Family & dependency ratios -------------------------------------------\nhf['children_ratio']   = hf['CNT_CHILDREN']    / (hf['CNT_FAM_MEMBERS'] + eps)\nhf['income_per_person']= hf['AMT_INCOME_TOTAL'] / (hf['CNT_FAM_MEMBERS'] + eps)\n\n# --- Stability ratios -------------------------------------------------------\nhf['employment_age_ratio'] = hf['years_employed'] / (hf['age'] + eps)\nhf['phone_change_ratio']   = hf['DAYS_LAST_PHONE_CHANGE'].abs() / (hf['age'] * 365.25 + eps)\n\n# --- Bureau request aggregation -------------------------------------------\nhf['bureau_requests'] = (\n    hf['AMT_REQ_CREDIT_BUREAU_DAY']  +\n    hf['AMT_REQ_CREDIT_BUREAU_WEEK'] +\n    hf['AMT_REQ_CREDIT_BUREAU_MON']  +\n    hf['AMT_REQ_CREDIT_BUREAU_YEAR']\n)\n\n# --- External score aggregation -------------------------------------------\nhf['ext_source_mean'] = hf[['EXT_SOURCE_1','EXT_SOURCE_2','EXT_SOURCE_3']].mean(axis=1)\nhf['ext_source_std']  = hf[['EXT_SOURCE_1','EXT_SOURCE_2','EXT_SOURCE_3']].std(axis=1)\nhf['ext_source_min']  = hf[['EXT_SOURCE_1','EXT_SOURCE_2','EXT_SOURCE_3']].min(axis=1)\n\n# --- Late-application flag (applications after 10pm = financial stress) ---\nhf['late_application_flag'] = ((hf['HOUR_APPR_PROCESS_START'] >= 22) |\n                                (hf['HOUR_APPR_PROCESS_START'] <= 5)).astype(int)\n\n# Drop raw day columns (already converted)\nhf.drop(['DAYS_BIRTH', 'DAYS_EMPLOYED'], axis=1, inplace=True, errors='ignore')\n\nprint(f\"  Home Credit features engineered: {hf.shape[1]} columns\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n## Step 4 — Credit Score Dataset: Segment-Level Behavioural Features\n\n### The Fix: Segment-Based Merge (Not Population Means)\n\nThe naive approach of assigning a single population mean to every applicant\ncreates constant columns that are immediately dropped. Instead we:\n\n1. Bin gig workers into **income quartiles** (Q1–Q4)\n2. Compute credit behaviour metrics **per quartile** from the Credit Score dataset\n3. Join back on income quartile → each applicant gets a **peer-group benchmark**\n\nThis gives 4 distinct values per feature instead of 1, preserving discriminative power.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Clean Credit Score dataset ─────────────────────────────────────────────\nCRED_NUMERIC = [\n    'Delay_from_due_date', 'Num_of_Delayed_Payment', 'Outstanding_Debt',\n    'Annual_Income', 'Total_EMI_per_month', 'Amount_invested_monthly'\n]\nfor col in CRED_NUMERIC:\n    cred[col] = pd.to_numeric(cred[col], errors='coerce')\n\n# ── Derive behavioural metrics per applicant in cred dataset ---------------\ncred['payment_discipline']       = 1 / (cred['Delay_from_due_date'].fillna(0) + 1)\ncred['obligation_fulfillment']   = 1 - (\n    cred['Num_of_Delayed_Payment'].fillna(0) /\n    (cred['Num_of_Delayed_Payment'].fillna(0).max() + 1)\n)\ncred['savings_ratio']    = cred['Amount_invested_monthly'] / (cred['Annual_Income'] / 12 + 1)\ncred['debt_income_ratio']= cred['Outstanding_Debt']        / (cred['Annual_Income']      + 1)\ncred['emi_income_ratio'] = cred['Total_EMI_per_month']     / (cred['Annual_Income'] / 12 + 1)\n\n# ── Bin cred by annual income into quartiles --------------------------------\ncred['income_quartile'] = pd.qcut(\n    cred['Annual_Income'].clip(lower=0),\n    q=4, labels=['Q1','Q2','Q3','Q4'], duplicates='drop'\n)\n\n# ── Compute quartile-level means -------------------------------------------\nCRED_FEATURES = [\n    'payment_discipline', 'obligation_fulfillment',\n    'savings_ratio', 'debt_income_ratio', 'emi_income_ratio'\n]\ncred_by_quartile = (\n    cred.groupby('income_quartile', observed=True)[CRED_FEATURES]\n    .mean()\n    .rename(columns=lambda c: f'cred_{c}')\n)\nprint(\"Credit Score — quartile-level feature means:\")\nprint(cred_by_quartile.round(4).to_string())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Map gig worker income to same quartile labels --------------------------\nhf['income_quartile'] = pd.qcut(\n    hf['AMT_INCOME_TOTAL'].clip(lower=0),\n    q=4, labels=['Q1','Q2','Q3','Q4'], duplicates='drop'\n)\n\n# ── Join credit features ---------------------------------------------------\nhf = hf.merge(cred_by_quartile, on='income_quartile', how='left')\n\nprint(f\"  Shape after Credit Score merge: {hf.shape}\")\nprint(f\"  New credit features: {[c for c in hf.columns if c.startswith('cred_')]}\")\n\n# ── Verify columns are NOT constant ---------------------------------------\nfor col in [c for c in hf.columns if c.startswith('cred_')]:\n    nuniq = hf[col].nunique()\n    print(f\"    {col:35s}  unique values: {nuniq}  ({'✅' if nuniq > 1 else '❌ CONSTANT'})\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n## Step 5 — Loan Default Dataset: DTI & Employment Signals\n\nSame segment-level approach: bin self-employed workers in the Loan Default\ndataset by income, compute loan-behaviour features per band, join to gig cohort.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Filter self-employed in loan dataset -----------------------------------\nloan_gig = loan[loan['EmploymentType'] == 'Self-employed'].copy()\n\n# ── Derived features -------------------------------------------------------\nloan_gig['loan_income_ratio'] = loan_gig['LoanAmount']   / (loan_gig['Income'] + 1)\nloan_gig['dti_ratio']         = loan_gig['DTIRatio']\nloan_gig['dti_flag']          = (loan_gig['DTIRatio'] > 0.40).astype(int)\nloan_gig['employment_years']  = loan_gig['MonthsEmployed'] / 12\nloan_gig['high_interest_flag']= (loan_gig['InterestRate'] > 15).astype(int)\nloan_gig['loan_default_rate'] = loan_gig['Default']   # 0/1 label\n\n# ── Bin by income into quartiles ------------------------------------------\nloan_gig['income_quartile'] = pd.qcut(\n    loan_gig['Income'].clip(lower=0),\n    q=4, labels=['Q1','Q2','Q3','Q4'], duplicates='drop'\n)\n\nLOAN_FEATURES = [\n    'loan_income_ratio', 'dti_ratio', 'dti_flag',\n    'employment_years', 'high_interest_flag', 'loan_default_rate'\n]\nloan_by_quartile = (\n    loan_gig.groupby('income_quartile', observed=True)[LOAN_FEATURES]\n    .mean()\n    .rename(columns=lambda c: f'loan_{c}')\n)\nprint(\"Loan Default — quartile-level feature means:\")\nprint(loan_by_quartile.round(4).to_string())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
